     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Jul 5, 2015 at 4:49 PM, Ayala Allon <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ayala...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Thank you Gabor.</font><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">I have one more question concerning this issue. if I do  what you explained (and of course the put the package name in Imports in the DESCRIPTION file), it means that when one uses my package the dependencies will also be installed if he doesn&#39;t have them already </font></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
