     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">and <code style=\"padding:1px;color:rgb(51,51,51);border-radius:4px;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">package::function() will exact the functions from the dependency right? </code></font></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>I am not sure what you mean here, sorry. If `package` is installed, and it has `function`, then yes `package::function` will work.</div><div><br></div><div>Gabor</div><div><br></div><div>ps. this is really an R-help question, it has not much to do with devtools.</div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
